# PRIME TIME: SHOWDOWN — game build settings (EXAMPLE, no real values).
#
# Every VITE_* value is compiled INTO the public game and visible to anyone: put only public
# settings here — never a password, token, key or anything from the server's pocketbase.env.
# Who may register (closed beta by invite, …) is NOT set here: the server decides it.
#
# ── Environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   (nothing)   the guest game, no accounts at all — what GitHub Pages builds today
#   local       PocketBase on this Mac (npm run backend) — only with `npm run dev:accounts`;
#               the file .env.accounts already sets it (and the mode alone is enough)
#   beta        the closed beta server (stage 2): https only
#   production  the public server after the closed beta: https only
#
# ── Stage 2 (not now): the published game talks to the closed beta server ─────────────────────
# Create `.env.production` (read by `npm run build`, also on GitHub Actions) with:
#
#   VITE_PRIME_ACCOUNTS=beta
#   VITE_PRIME_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.example
#
# A permanent API domain (not the server's IP) lets you move to another VPS later without a new
# game build. Without these two lines the build stays the guest game and makes no request.

VITE_PRIME_ACCOUNTS=
VITE_PRIME_API_URL=
